 | Text size and assistive technologies | Settings > Appearance > Text size offers Default, Large and Larger (1.0, 1.12 and 1.24 times every shared text style; default unchanged). macOS applies no Dynamic Type to SwiftUI text, so the app scales its own `TextStyle` tokens; the recording HUD and native menu keep their sizes and symbols stay fixed. Above Default, settings menu pickers draw their selected label at the scaled size and widen with it while the native picker stays available to VoiceOver and the keyboard. Pages, sheets, onboarding and License wrap rather than truncate at Larger in the fixed 784-point window; the sidebar microphone name may truncate with its full name in the tooltip. Every control has a VoiceOver name and state, decorative surfaces stay hidden, custom controls (switches, sliders, segmented choices, meters, waveform bars, model rows, History timeline and cards) expose roles and values, section titles are headings, and the sidebar reads before the page. Increase Contrast adds explicit edges to cards, controls, status dots, pill tags, meters and the Home hero; Reduce Motion removes spatial animation; Reduce Transparency keeps the opaque header. See `docs/accessibility.md`. |
 | Trigger Delay | Settings > Keyboard shortcuts offers a 0–1000 ms hold threshold, default 0, with direct entry and 50 ms steps. Short presses retain their normal action; a qualified hold starts dictation once. Hold release and Toggle stop remain immediate. Ordinary key events are buffered until the decision; modifier events pass through. Delayed shortcuts require Accessibility. Pending holds cancel on typing another key, chord/setup changes, focus changes and monitor interruption. Menu and automation actions remain immediate. |
 | Audio recording | Transcribe (named Meetings before 0.18.0) owns recording, imports, saved audio, transcript versions and interrupted-draft recovery. Every saved recording remains independently transcribable after restart. The compact Record Audio sheet selects app audio and optional microphone; its 320-point picker sizes its list to up to seven complete rows and preserves visible choices during refresh. Capture uses the microphone picker's shared linear ten-cell meters. New and recovered WAVs put the same microphone-plus-app mix in both stereo channels; existing files retain their bytes. The flow's primary buttons use the shared blue neumorphic button. Capture records gaps and stops at two hours without cursor insertion. With live preview on, the recording card shows a display-only Live transcript. Each library card shows the title, one metadata line, a status dot, a two-line preview and one player row ending in the next step (Transcribe, Resume or Open Transcript); versions, audio export, Finder and deletion sit in its actions menu. New transcripts take the library title (Recording or Imported Recording) instead of repeating the date. The transcript editor has a fixed header and footer around Summary, Speakers and one Transcript card, and opens without a focused title. See `meeting-recording.md`. |
